userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: A tangent line at P is the limiting position of the secant line through P and a second point Q as Q slides along the curve toward P, and this single limiting definition reproduces the classical tangent to a circle.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): The tangent line is not a separate construction — it is simply the limiting position of secant lines PQ as Q approaches P, one definition that works for any smooth curve and reduces to the usual tangent on a circle.
DEMO STEPS: 5 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

